  "id": "0c5e6bd6-613c-5906-80b7-ca7e2a76dad9",
  "slug": "blueberry-cherry-pie",
  "name": "Blueberry Cherry Pie",
  "recipe_type": "dessert",
  "brief_description": "Who would have thought? Blueberries and cherries in the same pie. But they \u2018re divine together. You \u2018ll have to pit the cherries, but it should be a labor of love. The berries are sugared, dusted with flour and cinnamon, and dotted with butter. The oven takes care of the rest.",
  "cuisine": "U.S.",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Mix sugar, flour, and cinnamon in large bowl. Add fruit. Add lemon juice, and stir well."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Pour into a 9 inch unbaked pie shell. Dot with the butter or margarine. Cover with top crust and flute edges. Cut small slits in the top."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Bake at 375 degrees F (190 degrees C) for 1 hour. I put a baking sheet under mine to catch any liquid that might bubble over."
    }
  ],
